At C, phase difference

\phi=\frac{2 \pi}{\alpha}\left(\ell_2-\ell_1\right)=80 \pi

Hence for maximum intensity will appear at C . Now for minimum intensity at C

\begin{aligned}
& (\mu-1) \mathrm{t}=\frac{\lambda}{2} \\
& \mathrm{t}=\frac{\mathrm{t}}{2(\mu-1)}=500 \mathrm{~nm}
\end{aligned}

